cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Suicide Research Evidence Database (SRED): An Open Bibliographic
  Infrastructure for Scientometric Research on Suicide and Suicide Prevention
message: >-
  If you use this database, code, or derived data, please cite both the
  software (this file) and the accompanying article.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yunyu118/suicide-research-evidence-database"

authors:
  - family-names: Xiao
    given-names: Yunyu
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Population Health Sciences, Weill Cornell Medicine,
      Cornell University
    email: yux4008@med.cornell.edu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0479-1781"

abstract: >-
  SRED is an open, fully reproducible bibliographic infrastructure for the
  study of suicide research knowledge production. It integrates PubMed/MEDLINE,
  Europe PMC, and OpenAlex into a deduplicated corpus of suicide-focused
  scholarship published between 1989 and 2025, combining a venue-based core of
  dedicated suicidology journals with a topical sweep across all other
  publication venues. Abstracts are classified by scientific communication
  type, empirical status, and research methodology using a distantly
  supervised classifier trained on human MEDLINE indexing, with an
  interchangeable local large language model backend. SRED additionally
  extracts suicide-specific fields absent from every existing bibliographic
  database: position on the prevention continuum, suicide-related outcome
  construct, study population, study design, lethal means focus, and social
  determinants of health.

keywords:
  - suicide
  - suicide prevention
  - suicidology
  - bibliometrics
  - scientometrics
  - social determinants of health
  - open science
  - health informatics
  - large language models

